# What never enters a build context (ADR-0059 §4).
#
# All three images build from the repository root, because a pnpm workspace
# cannot be installed from one app's directory — the lockfile, the workspace
# file and every internal package it links are at the top. That makes this file
# load-bearing rather than cosmetic: without it every build would ship the
# developer's `node_modules`, their `.env` and the whole git history, and
# invalidate its own cache on any of them.

# Installed inside the image, from the committed lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output and caches, all of which the image regenerates.
dist
**/dist
# The declarations-only emit `tsc -b` writes (D14.9, ADR-0062 §3). No image
# stage resolves to it; the type-check inside the build regenerates it.
dist-types
**/dist-types
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.tanstack

# Every env file, including the committed examples. Nothing in a build reads
# one: the API takes its configuration at run time (ADR-0004) and the SPAs take
# theirs as build arguments (ADR-0059 §4, and see the note in each SPA's
# Dockerfile about why Vite forces that). Excluding the whole family — rather
# than `.env` alone — is what stops a developer's file, or `apps/api/.env.test`
# and its committed signing key, from riding into an image.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The Playwright storage state, which holds a live refresh cookie
# (`.gitignore` says so). It only ever reaches the discarded build stage, but a
# credential has no business in a build context or a builder cache.
**/e2e/.auth

# History and tooling that no build step reads.
.git
.github
.claude
docs
**/*.log
